&lt;p class=&quot;c76&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;We are a next generation solutions provider, delivering mission success across government, healthcare, and commercial industries. Iron Bow relies on our&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;passionate people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;long standing partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;, and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;strategic thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to solve your most critical challenges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether we team with clients, colleagues, or partners, we put each other first. It’s &lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Iron Bow Way.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Iron Bow is seeking an Sr. Service Provider Network Engineer to provide technical leadership, subject matter expertise, and engineering oversight supporting Headquarters Pacific Air Forces (PACAF) A6. This position plays a critical role in the operation, optimization, and expansion of the PACAF BlackCore network, leveraging advanced Cisco SRv6 and Crosswork technologies to support mission-critical communications across the Pacific Area of Responsibility (AOR).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate will possess deep expertise in enterprise networking, WAN technologies, network security, and DoD cybersecurity requirements while serving as a trusted technical advisor to government stakeholders and senior leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;HOW YOU’LL MAKE AN IMPACT&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide engineering oversight and operational support for the PACAF BlackCore SRv6 network environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, optimize, and maintain Cisco SRv6 and Crosswork solutions supporting mission-critical operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain comprehensive documentation of SRv6 configurations, network policies, standards, and operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver technical training and knowledge transfer to PACAF personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ongoing maintenance, modernization, and expansion of the BlackCore network infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical lead during network incidents, troubleshooting efforts, and service restoration activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor network performance and optimize configurations for bandwidth utilization, application-aware routing, resiliency, and failover capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide advanced troubleshooting for connectivity, performance, security, and routing issues within SRv6 environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Government with Risk Management Framework (RMF) activities and Accreditation &amp;amp; Authorization (A&amp;amp;A) documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, review, and maintain RMF deliverables, including:
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Security Plans (SSPs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ports, Protocols, and Services Management (PPSM) documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Control validation artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STIG compliance documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan of Action &amp;amp; Milestones (POA&amp;amp;M)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Topology Documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and develop A&amp;amp;A artifacts in accordance with Authorizing Official (AO) requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide recommendations for risk mitigation strategies and follow-on corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support network architecture planning and implementation efforts across PACAF Main Operating Bases (MOBs) and Geographically Separated Units (GSUs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and deliver technical briefings to government leadership, technical teams, and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across engineering, cybersecurity, operations, and government teams to ensure successful mission execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;SKILLS THAT DRIVE SUCCESS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret (TS) Security Clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of hands-on experience supporting Cisco SRv6 solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Air Force Cyber architecture and PACAF organizational structures, including MOBs and GSUs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting DoD cybersecurity requirements, RMF processes, ATO packages, and compliance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collecting, developing, and maintaining Accreditation &amp;amp; Authorization (A&amp;amp;A) artifacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced understanding of enterprise networking concepts and architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional-level proficiency with:
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TCP/IP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DNS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;VPNs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;VLANs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSPF&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BGP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MPLS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SRv6&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of WAN technologies and network optimization strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading network implementation, deployment, maintenance, and modernization efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of network security principles and cybersecurity best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to diagnose and resolve complex networking and security issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining detailed network design documentation and diagrams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud networking environments, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and collaboration tools, including SharePoint and Microsoft Teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience briefing technical information to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to brief senior leaders and large audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, collaboration, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Certification Requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Must possess one (1) certification meeting DoD 8140 Advanced Cyber Workforce requirements, including but not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP-ISSEP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CySA+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GSLC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GSNA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GCSA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FITSP-A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPTE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;AND&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Must meet DoD 8570.01-M Information Assurance Technical (IAT) Level III requirements through one (1) of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CASP+ CE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CCSP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;WHAT SETS &lt;em&gt;YOU&lt;/em&gt; APART&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cisco Certified Network Professional (CCNP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juniper Networks Certified Professional (JNCIP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting large-scale DoD enterprise networking environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Cisco Crosswork platforms and automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Air Force and PACAF mission environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading enterprise network transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software-defined networking (SDN) architectures and automation technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Primary work location is Headquarters Pacific Air Forces (PACAF) A6, Oahu, Hawaii.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel throughout the PACAF Area of Responsibility to support Main Operating Bases (MOBs) and Geographically Separated Units (GSUs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel may be required up to 10% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;WHY YOU’LL LOVE IT&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to support critical national defense and Indo-Pacific mission operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cutting-edge networking technologies, including Cisco SRv6 and Crosswork.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key technical advisor to senior military and government leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with highly skilled engineers and cybersecurity professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to the modernization and resilience of Air Force communications infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation, comprehensive benefits, and professional development opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFIT INFORMATION&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The salary range for this position is $160,000-$180,000/yr. This range reflects the anticipated base pay for the position and is not a guarantee of final compensation. Actual compensation will be determined based on factors including experience, skills, education, location, contract requirements, and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Bow Technologies reserves the right to fill this role at a different level, depending on qualifications and organizational priorities. This range represents only one component of Iron Bow’s total compensation package. An overview of our benefits is available on our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-EC1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;c68&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c69&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER COMMITMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;c68&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;Iron Bow Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to the principle of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment.&amp;nbsp; All employment decisions at Iron Bow are based on relevant business considerations, such as operational needs, job requirements and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or gender expression, pregnancy, national origin, age, disability, status as a protected veteran or any other characteristic prohibited by law.&amp;nbsp;Iron Bow will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;c76&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;Iron Bow Technologies is for people who believe&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;trust is paramount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;transformation is embraced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;, and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;the future is here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;because&lt;strong&gt; &quot;What we do matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;!&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;c76&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;We are a next generation solutions provider, delivering mission success across government, healthcare, and commercial industries. Iron Bow relies on our&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;passionate people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;long standing partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;, and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;strategic thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to solve your most critical challenges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether we team with clients, colleagues, or partners, we put each other first. It’s &lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Iron Bow Way.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Vice President, Security &amp;amp; Observability&lt;/strong&gt; is responsible for defining, building, and executing the strategy for the company&#39;s Security &amp;amp; Observability business, known as VSO360.&amp;nbsp; Reporting to the Chief Growth Officer, this leader will own the strategy, business development, go-to-market approach, and growth of the Security &amp;amp; Observability portfolio. The VP will bring deep knowledge of the security and observability markets, extensive Splunk experience, strong technical credibility, and the business acumen required to translate technology capabilities into differentiated customer outcomes and sustainable growth. This is a highly collaborative leadership role operating across Sales, CTO, Marketing, Service Delivery, Alliances, and other functions. The VP will directly lead a team of Business Development professionals aligned to the company&#39;s business units and will work closely with supporting CTO and Service Delivery resources to develop solutions, capabilities, and services that address customer needs.&amp;nbsp; &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position will be based in the Washington DC Metropolitan area - Herndon, VA or Annapolis, MD is preferred.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;HOW YOU’LL MAKE AN IMPACT&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy &amp;amp; Business Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own the overall strategy for the Security &amp;amp; Observability business, including the VSO360 initiative.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the vision, market positioning, growth priorities and roadmap for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging market trends, technologies, customer requirements, and competitive dynamics and translate them into actionable business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the markets, customer segments, use cases, and solutions where the company can establish differentiated positions and drive meaningful growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish business plans, performance metrics, pipeline, and growth targets and maintain accountability for results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a scalable business that combines technology, professional services, and partner capabilities to address customer requirements with branded market awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully optimize the sales force to represent the Security &amp;amp; Observability portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create market leadership supporting the Splunk transition into the broader Cisco portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Development &amp;amp; Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of three Business Development professionals supporting the company&#39;s business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute business development strategies that generate pipeline, accelerate opportunities, and expand relationships with existing and new customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business unit and sales leadership to identify strategic accounts and opportunities where Security &amp;amp; Observability capabilities can create differentiated value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with customers and prospects to understand business and technical challenges, shape requirements, develop solutions, and communicate the value of the company&#39;s capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support major pursuits from opportunity identification and qualification through solution development, proposal, and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Splunk &amp;amp; Technology Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior business and technology leader for the company&#39;s broader Security &amp;amp; Observability portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply extensive Splunk experience to develop differentiated solutions, services, and go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong understanding of the Splunk platform, ecosystem, partner programs, competitive landscape, and evolving product portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customer data environments and how security, observability, IT operations, and related capabilities can transform enterprise data into actionable intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with CTO resources to develop architectures, solutions, demonstrations, intellectual property, and technical differentiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate adjacent and complementary technologies that can expand the capabilities and addressable market of the Security &amp;amp; Observability practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Services &amp;amp; Capability Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Service Delivery leadership to develop and mature professional, managed, and lifecycle services supporting the Security &amp;amp; Observability portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer requirements and market opportunities into repeatable offerings and scalable delivery capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define required skills, certifications, methodologies, tools, and investments necessary to support growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment between what is sold, what customers need, and what the organization can successfully deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to create recurring revenue and long-term customer relationships through managed and ongoing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-Market &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Marketing to develop market positioning, messaging, campaigns, thought leadership, customer success stories, and demand-generation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales leadership to develop enablement programs that help sellers identify, qualify, position, and advance Security &amp;amp; Observability opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across business units to establish a consistent strategy while adapting offerings and go-to-market approaches to the requirements of different customer segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-level relationships with Splunk, Cisco and complementary technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company at customer meetings, industry events, partner engagements, conferences, and executive briefings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create alignment across Sales, CTO, Marketing, Service Delivery, Operations, and executive leadership around priorities and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Managerial &amp;amp; Inspirational Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage three Business Development professionals aligned to and supporting the company&#39;s business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic and cross-functional leadership to a broader virtual team of CTO, solution architecture, engineering, marketing, and Service Delivery resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be highly effective at leading through influence and creating alignment across organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;SKILLS THAT DRIVE SUCCESS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant leadership experience in cybersecurity, observability, data intelligence, IT operations, or related technology markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with Splunk, including a strong understanding of its technology, use cases, ecosystem, customers, and go-to-market model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build, grow, or significantly expand a technology or services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong combination of technical depth and business acumen, with the ability to operate effectively with engineers and architects as well as sales executives, customers, partners, and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the security and observability markets and the convergence of data, security operations, infrastructure, applications, cloud, and IT operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing business strategies, go-to-market plans, and growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success developing pipeline and supporting complex enterprise sales pursuits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building technology-enabled professional and/or managed services offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional teams and influence resources outside of direct reporting relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication and presentation skills with the ability to articulate complex technical concepts in business and customer-outcome terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing senior-level relationships with customers and strategic technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership skills with demonstrated success developing and managing high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;WHAT SETS &lt;em&gt;YOU&lt;/em&gt; APART&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships within Splunk and the broader Splunk partner and customer ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or building a Splunk-focused business, practice, or center of excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across both security and observability use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing recurring revenue, managed services, or as-a-service offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across federal, state, local and commercial markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Splunk, cybersecurity, cloud, or observability certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a highly external customer facing operating cadence with significant time meeting in person with customers, prospects and Splunk/Cisco leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must reside in the Washington DC Metropolitan with the ability to travel regularly (local and nationally) as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;WHY YOU’LL LOVE IT&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be part of a mission-critical team that directly impacts our ability to deliver competitive, compliant and innovative solutions to our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be a key contributor to Iron Bows’s transformational shift in how we deliver value to both customers and employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will have the pleasure of working with passionate professionals in a culture that fosters a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS INFORMATION: &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The initial base salary range for this position is $190,000 - $250,000&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;In addition to base salary, this role offers a &lt;strong&gt;competitive on-target earnings (OTE) structure, with strong upside potential&lt;/strong&gt;. Our compensation plans are designed to reward success, drive growth, and recognize the impact our sales teams make in the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Iron Bow, we invest in our people and their success. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that may include medical, dental, and vision coverage, a 401(k) plan, paid time off, and additional wellness and financial benefits. An overview of our benefits is available on our careers page.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-MA1 #LI-Virginia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;c68&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c69&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER COMMITMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;c68&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;Iron Bow Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to the principle of equal employment opportunity for all employees and to providing employees with a work environment free of discrimination and harassment.&amp;nbsp; All employment decisions at Iron Bow are based on relevant business considerations, such as operational needs, job requirements and individual qualifications, without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or gender expression, pregnancy, national origin, age, disability, status as a protected veteran or any other characteristic prohibited by law.&amp;nbsp;Iron Bow will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;c76&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;Iron Bow Technologies is for people who believe&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;trust is paramount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;transformation is embraced&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;, and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c77&quot;&gt;the future is here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;because&lt;strong&gt; &quot;What we do matters&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;!&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;c76&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;We are a next generation solutions provider, delivering mission success across government, healthcare, and commercial industries. Iron Bow relies on our&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;passionate people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;,&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;long standing partnerships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;, and&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;strategic thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c19&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;to solve your most critical challenges.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether we team with clients, colleagues, or partners, we put each other first. It’s &lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Iron Bow Way.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Iron Bow Technologies is seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Principal Telecommunications Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to support the design, engineering, implementation, and optimization of complex voice and data telecommunications solutions for our customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will serve as a senior technical expert responsible for evaluating existing telecommunications infrastructure, developing innovative network architectures, and identifying opportunities to improve service delivery, reliability, and cost efficiency. You will work closely with customers, telecommunications carriers, service providers, and technical teams to develop and implement solutions that meet operational and business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate brings extensive experience in IP telephony, voice and data network engineering, carrier services, and technical project management, along with a strong understanding of emerging telecommunications technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW YOU&#39;LL MAKE AN IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate existing telecommunications and operations support systems to identify opportunities for modernization, improved performance, and cost efficiencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design, engineering, and implementation of voice and data telecommunications solutions, including network interfaces, system integrations, and supporting infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assess emerging technologies and recommend telecommunications platforms, network architectures, and solutions that align with customer requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide Tier 3 engineering support for complex telecommunications and network incidents, including troubleshooting, root-cause analysis, corrective actions, and resolution of escalated issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate carrier-provided network services, telecommunications architectures, and service options to ensure optimal performance, reliability, and cost effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop detailed engineering designs, network configurations, process flows, and technical documentation supporting system implementation and ongoing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and execute voice integration and failover testing plans to validate system functionality, reliability, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct telecommunications billing audits, identify discrepancies, and work with carriers to resolve billing issues and recover applicable credits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with telecommunications carriers, service providers, and internal stakeholders to coordinate service implementations, monitor delivery timelines, and ensure compliance with contractual requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop project management plans, including implementation schedules, resource estimates, cost projections, and risk mitigation strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify opportunities to introduce advanced telecommunications capabilities while improving operational efficiency and reducing costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare and present technical recommendations, strategic analyses, Statements of Work (SOWs), and management reports to customers and key stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide technical guidance, training, and customer support throughout the implementation and ongoing management of telecommunications solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;c69&quot;&gt;SKILLS THAT DRIVE SUCCESS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;3 3 []&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum &lt;strong&gt;15 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in voice and data network engineering, telecommunications architecture, and related business operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum &lt;strong&gt;10 years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; designing and implementing IP telephony systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum &lt;strong&gt;10 years of project management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, preferably within a client-facing technical services environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of telecommunications infrastructure, network architecture, and carrier-provided transport services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of LAN/WAN and VoIP technologies, including MPLS, BGP, SIP, IMS, and related network protocols.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
